  <!-- Custom Battle only (SubModule.xml registers this file for CustomGame, before the lords node).
       Each entry is a bare stub for a vanilla SandBox lord that TAOM rebuilds in lords.xslt. SandBox
       registers its lords.xml for Campaign and CampaignStoryMode only, so in a Custom Battle those lords
       do not exist and the lords.xslt template has nothing to rebuild. The engine applies each node's
       XSLT to everything merged before it (MBObjectManager.CreateMergedXmlFile, v1.5.7), so lords.xslt
       turns each stub into the full character: name, race, face, skills and equipment all come from the
       template, none from here. The culture is repeated only because NPCCharacters.xsd requires the
       attribute; keep it equal to the template's.
       An id may have a stub when lords.xslt has a whole-lord template for it and characters/lords.xml
       has no row for it; CustomBattleLordStubsTests checks both. Outside a campaign these lords are
       named by custom_battle/custom_battle_commanders.json, fords_of_war/factions.json,
       long_defeat/fortresses.json (playerTroop lord_4_1), hero_auras/hero_auras.json and
       SeatTrialRoster.Hero (lord_1_9), among others; the default commanders and the muster hero
       lists pick the rest by culture.
       Until #648, 176 vanilla-id lords reached Custom Battle through their characters/lords.xml rows.
       When those rows were folded into the lords.xslt templates, each got a stub here (ten in the
       sections above, the rest in the last section), so Custom Battle keeps every lord it had.
       CustomBattleCommandersShippedDataTests checks that every culture it offers resolves a commander
       of its own. -->

